      "fact_text": {
        "text": "The for‑each loop has a limitation that it can only iterate forward, so it cannot iterate over an array from the end to the beginning.",
        "refs": ["Q0001"],
        "claims": [
          {
            "text": "The for‑each loop can only iterate forward and cannot iterate from the end to the beginning of an array.",
            "basis": "explicit",
            "availability": "SOURCE_SUPPORTED",
            "literal_kind": "verbal",
            "instructional_role": "prerequisite",
            "refs": ["Q0001"],
            "related_refs": []
          }
        ]
      },
      "fact_type": null
    },
    {
      "fact_text": {
        "text": "The for‑each loop does not provide access to the index of each item; only the loop variable holding the item value is available.",
        "refs": ["Q0005", "Q0006"],
        "claims": [
          {
            "text": "The for‑each loop does not give access to the index of each element, only the element value via the loop variable.",
            "basis": "explicit",
            "availability": "SOURCE_SUPPORTED",
            "literal_kind": "verbal",
            "instructional_role": "prerequisite",
            "refs": ["Q0005", "Q0006"],
            "related_refs": []
          }
        ]
      },
      "fact_type": null
    },
    {
      "fact_text": {
        "text": "In a traditional for loop you can access both the index and the actual item, e.g., using i as the index and fruits[i] as the item.",
        "refs": ["Q0007", "Q0008"],
        "claims": [
          {
            "text": "A traditional for loop allows access to both the index (i) and the item (fruits[i]).",
            "basis": "explicit",
            "availability": "SOURCE_SUPPORTED",
            "literal_kind": "verbal",
            "instructional_role": "prerequisite",
            "refs": ["Q0007", "Q0008"],
            "related_refs": []
          }
        ]
      },
      "fact_type": null
    },
    {
      "fact_text": {
        "text": "If you need the index of each element, you should use a for loop rather than a for‑each loop; otherwise the for‑each loop is easier to use.",
        "refs": ["Q0009"],
        "claims": [
          {
            "text": "Use a for loop when the index is needed; otherwise the for‑each loop is simpler.",
            "basis": "explicit",
            "availability": "SOURCE_SUPPORTED",
            "literal_kind": "verbal",
            "instructional_role": "correct_demonstration",
            "refs": ["Q0009"],
            "related_refs": []
          }
        ]
      },
      "fact_type": null
    }
  ],
